  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Lang\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Lang\n       Program: commons-lang\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Lang/Lang.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-lang.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Lang/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 61\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Lang-52\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\nc22d9d59e5b86c33f91d7fa93d71cdc514c2edd9\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2007-10-26 06:08:54 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nLANG-363\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/LANG-363\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.lang.StringEscapeUtilsTest::testEscapeJavaScript\n   --> junit.framework.ComparisonFailure: expected:<...ipt>alert(\\'aaa\\');<[\\]/script>\\';> but was:<...ipt>alert(\\'aaa\\');<[]/script>\\';>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.lang.StringEscapeUtils\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: StringEscapeUtils.escapeJavaScript() method did not escape '/' into '\\/', it will make IE render page uncorrectly\nType: Bug | Priority: Minor | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nIf Javascripts including'/', IE will parse the scripts uncorrectly, actually '/' should be escaped to '\\/'.\nFor example, document.getElementById(\"test\").value = '<script>alert(\\'aaa\\');</script>';this expression will make IE render page uncorrect, it should be document.getElementById(\"test\").value = '<script>alert(\\'aaa\\');<\\/script>';\n\nBtw, Spring's JavascriptEscape behavor is correct.\nTry  to run below codes, you will find the difference:\n  String s = \"<script>alert('aaa');</script>\";\n  String str = org.springframework.web.util.JavaScriptUtils.javaScriptEscape(s);\n  System.out.println(\"Spring JS Escape : \"+str);\n  str = org.apache.commons.lang.StringEscapeUtils.escapeJavaScript(s);\n  System.out.println(\"Apache Common Lang JS Escape : \"+ str);\n\nComments:\n\n[Scott Bassin]: Here's a patch that should fix the issue described.  Also included is an extra assertion in testEscapeJavaScript of StringEscapeUtilsTest.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Heh - I even had a play with this when looking at the Spring one: http://opensource.atlassian.com/projects/spring/browse/SPR-1754\n\nNot sure why I didn't submit a fix, probably too green with Spring at the time.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Thanks again Scott (and Situ for reporting it), patch applied:\n\nsvn ci -m \"Applying Scott Bassin's fix and test from LANG-363\" src/test/org/apache/commons/lang/StringEscapeUtilsTest.java src/java/org/apache/commons/lang/StringEscapeUtils.java\n\nSending        src/java/org/apache/commons/lang/StringEscapeUtils.java\nSending        src/test/org/apache/commons/lang/StringEscapeUtilsTest.java\nTransmitting file data ..\nCommitted revision 588534.\n\n[ggregory@seagullsw.com]: fix typo in summary field\n\n[Henri Yandell]: See LANG-437 for conversation about rolling this fix back. There are user complaints on the list that the change is causing problems.",
  "fix_diff": ""
